<section class="editorial-page" aria-labelledby="privacy-title">
    <span class="marquee-kicker">Your choices</span>
    <h1 id="privacy-title">Privacy</h1>
    <p>Eat My Movies is run by James in the United Kingdom. For privacy questions or requests, email <a href="mailto:eatmymovies@hotmail.com">eatmymovies@hotmail.com</a>.</p>
    <h2>Where the site runs</h2>
    <p>The website runs on SmarterASP.NET hosting. Its film lists and editorial content are stored in a Microsoft Azure database. SmarterASP.NET generates daily IIS access logs for website requests, which may include technical information such as your IP address.</p>
    <h2>Information you give us</h2>
    <p>If you email us, we use your address and message to respond and manage your enquiry. Please avoid sending sensitive information. We delete routine contact emails within 12 months of our last reply, or within 12 months of receiving your message if we do not reply. You can ask us to delete your message sooner by emailing us.</p>
    <h2>Optional tracking</h2>
    <p>With your choice, we use Google Analytics to understand visits. It may use cookies or similar browser storage and receive information about your device and activity on this site. We do not load it until you accept optional tracking. Your choice is saved in your browser's local storage so we can remember it. You can reject it or change your choice using “Tracking preferences” in the footer. Our basis for this optional tracking is your consent. Hotjar is currently disabled.</p>
    <p>Google Analytics is set to retain event data for two months and user data for 14 months. New activity resets the 14-month period for a user identifier. These settings do not limit the retention of Google's standard aggregated reports. Google signals is off, and our Google Ads account is disabled.</p>
    <p>See the <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google privacy policy</a> for information about its processing, retention and international transfers.</p>
    <h2>Essential site functions and external content</h2>
    <p>The admin area uses an authentication cookie to keep its administrator signed in. It expires after eight hours, although activity can renew that period. Movie posters and details may be requested from TMDb, and following a streaming link takes you to an external site. Those providers may receive technical information, such as your IP address, when your browser connects to them.</p>
    <h2>Your rights</h2>
    <p>You can contact us to ask about personal information we hold about you, request correction or deletion, or withdraw tracking consent. You can also raise a concern with the <a href="https://ico.org.uk/make-a-complaint/" rel="noopener noreferrer">UK Information Commissioner’s Office</a>.</p>
</section>
